    "title": "otosora v0.7.1",
    "notes": "# Otosora 0.7.1\n\n## Otosora on Windows and Linux\n- New desktop app for Windows (`otosora-v0.7.1-windows-x64.zip`) and Linux (`otosora-v0.7.1-linux-x64.tar.gz`), with the same library, streaming, downloads, lyrics and playlists as the phone app.\n- A desktop layout: a sidebar with your playlists, pages that open in the middle, a now playing panel with synced lyrics and what plays next, and a player bar with seek and volume.\n- Songs come from your Music folder. Add more folders in Settings → Music folders.\n- Space plays and pauses, Ctrl+←/→ change songs, Ctrl+↑/↓ change the volume. Right-click a song for its actions.\n- Windows: previous, play/pause and next under the taskbar thumbnail, the media overlay for keyboard media keys, and the visualizer, which listens only to Otosora's own sound.\n- Linux: media keys and the desktop's media panel work through MPRIS.\n\n## Installing on desktop\n- Windows: unzip anywhere and run `otosora.exe`.\n- Linux: extract the archive and run `./install.sh`. It adds Otosora to the applications menu. Audio needs libmpv (Fedora: `mpv-libs` from RPM Fusion, Ubuntu: `libmpv2`).\n- Desktop versions do not update themselves yet. Download the new archive to update.\n\n## Phone\n- The line being sung now sits in the middle of the lyrics.\n",
